      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the Greatest Common Divisor (GCD) of 342 and 285. The GCD is the largest number that divides both numbers without leaving a remainder.\n\nStep 1: Prime Factorization\nFirst, we factorize 342 and 285 into their prime factors:\n342 = 2 × 3 × 3 × 19\n285 = 3 × 5 × 19\n\nStep 2: Identify the Common Prime Factors\nNow, we identify the common prime factors:\n3 and 19\n\nStep 3: Calculate the GCD\nThe GCD is the product of the common prime factors with the lowest exponents:\nGCD = 3 × 19 = 57\n\nTherefore, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is 57.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{57}",
